From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:28:34 -0400
Subject: fix: the right edge, older sidebar files, essentials, and an F6 crash

Sidebar Y39: with the sidebar hidden on the right, a rest on the close
button of a maximized window on Windows revealed the sidebar over it. The
reveal edge now starts under the frame's own buttons in the top-right
corner.

Sidebar file Sf2: a file Stedding wrote before its tabs kept a token named
each tab by the session's number, which is new at every launch, so each
import of such a file added all its tabs again. Those ids are remembered in
the profile, as Arc's are, and the file adds its tabs once.

Import I11: a Space's own essentials imported into a Space here that has no
session of its own went into the shared row, counted against that Space's
own (none), and filled it past twelve. They now count as shared ones.

Pane focus (F6): Chromium's own lookup of the window's contents view may
find none, and the bubble search used it unchecked: an access violation on
Windows. It is checked, as the same file does a few lines above.

Why: a review of the sidebar on the right (S-96) and of Export all Spaces
(S-282).
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
